From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 12:17:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: kbuild: fix dtbs_install race when parents are
 shared

dtbs_install installs every dtb with "install -D", relying on it to
create the destination subdirectory. Under make -j, the dtbs sharing a
directory are dispatched concurrently, so several install processes race
to create that one parent.

GNU coreutils absorbs the resulting EEXIST and carries on. uutils, which
Ubuntu now ships as coreutils, treats it as fatal:

  INSTALL .../device-tree/actions/s700-cubieboard7.dtb
  INSTALL .../device-tree/actions/s900-bubblegum-96.dtb
  install: cannot create directory '.../device-tree/actions'
  make[4]: *** [scripts/Makefile.dtbinst:23: .../s900-bubblegum-96.dtb] Error 1

arm64 trips over this on the very first such directory and fails to
build. A loop of 100 paired installs into one fresh directory reproduces
it 25 times with uutils and never with GNU coreutils.

Create the parent with "mkdir -p", which is required to succeed on an
existing directory, and drop the now-redundant -D. The same loop is
clean over 100 iterations afterwards.

Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00215
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@acfb36c87f8d8d1f559feb7e12e4f3a206d70047
---
 scripts/Makefile.dtbinst | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/Makefile.dtbinst b/scripts/Makefile.dtbinst
index 9d920419a62c..3d409d9db7e4 100644
--- a/scripts/Makefile.dtbinst
+++ b/scripts/Makefile.dtbinst
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ include $(srctree)/scripts/Kbuild.include
 dst := $(INSTALL_DTBS_PATH)
 
 quiet_cmd_dtb_install = INSTALL $@
-      cmd_dtb_install = install -D -m 0644 $< $@
+      cmd_dtb_install = mkdir -p $(dir $@) && install -m 0644 $< $@
 
 $(dst)/%: $(obj)/%
 	$(call cmd,dtb_install)
